  "player_hint_1_en": "Look at Basil: every square he could still use shares a row or column with row 6, column 1. So nobody else can stand at row 6, column 1, or Basil would have nowhere to go. Look at Elsa: every square she could still use shares a row or column with row 4, column 6. So nobody else can stand at row 4, column 6, or Elsa would have nowhere to go. Alma and Dinah can't share a row or column, so Alma's clue (\"She was exactly one row north of Dinah.\") rules out more squares for Alma. The same kind of reasoning rules out a few more squares. So Dinah (D) must be at row 4, column 2. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_2_en": "With the rows and columns of Dinah crossed out, only one square is left for Basil that fits his clue (\"He was the only person beside a crate.\"). So Basil (B) must be at row 5, column 1. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_3_en": "With the rows and columns of Dinah and Basil crossed out, only one square is left for Elsa that fits her clue (\"She was sitting in a chair in the Counter.\"). So Elsa (E) must be at row 2, column 6. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_4_en": "All of Alma's squares are in row 3, so nobody else can use it. So Cedric (C) must be at row 1, column 3. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_5_en": "Gus's clue (\"Someone else in his area was beside a sign.\") needs the person beside a sign in Gus's area on a square that does not share his row or column; that rules out squares for Gus. So Gus (G) must be at row 9, column 5. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_6_en": "Who can be the person beside a sign in Gus's area? Only Howard, because nobody else can still reach a square that fits Gus's clue (\"Someone else in his area was beside a sign.\"). That rules out Howard's other squares. So Howard (H) must be at row 6, column 4. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_7_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Fergus that fits his clue (\"He was exactly two columns east of Elsa.\"). So Fergus (F) must be at row 7, column 8. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_8_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Valerie. So Valerie (the victim) must be at row 8, column 9. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_9_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Alma that fits her clue (\"She was exactly one row north of Dinah.\"). So Alma (A) must be at row 3, column 7. Cross out her row and column. Fergus is the only person in the Parking Lot with Valerie, so Fergus is the murderer!"
 },
